    "updated_at": "2022-12-25T08:07:44Z",
    "body": "With the PR in `gitoxide` merged, we could provide you with a `starship` binary that instead of panicking would provide the path of the offending file. That way, it might be possible for you to provide that single file instead. That could be integrated into `gitoxide`'s test suite to assure it is handled as well as possible given that it's probably defective in some way. \r\n\r\nOnce the path is revealed, I would also be interested to see what `git cat-file <hash-of-corrupted-object>` shows - maybe git can read it, or has more interesting information to reveal?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
