    "created_at": "2022-12-25T09:31:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-12-25T09:31:58Z",
    "body": "Find below, the steps to reproduce this issue:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ngit clone https://github.com/Byron/gitoxide.git\r\ncd gitoxide\r\ngit checkout -b assertWhileRebasing\r\necho \"Hello, World\" > bug.txt\r\ngit add bug.txt\r\ngit commit -m \"chore: add a new file\"\r\ngit rebase -i main\r\n\r\n...\r\n... Replace `pick 7ae00dc7a chore: add a new file` with `edit 7ae00dc7a chore: add a new file` to edit the commit ...\r\n...\r\n\r\n# Now the trick is to edit the file containing the commit which is currently rebased\r\nmv .git/objects/7a/e00dc7a579d14cfa15186f50360a92deecb1b1 .git/objects/7a/e00dc7a579d14cfa15186f50360a92deecb1b1.backup\r\ntouch .git/objects/7a/e00dc7a579d14cfa15186f50360a92deecb1b1\r\n\r\n# Here the backtrace should appear\r\nthread '<unnamed>' panicked at 'assertion failed: `(left != right)`\r\n  left: `BufError`,\r\n right: `BufError`: Buffer errors might mean we encountered huge headers', /github/home/.cache/Homebrew/cargo_cache/registry/src/github.com-1ecc6299db9ec823/git-odb-0.37.0/src/store_impls/loose/find.rs:156:9\r\nnote: run with `RUST_BACKTRACE=1` environment variable to display a backtrace\r\nthread '<unnamed>' panicked at 'assertion failed: `(left != right)`\r\n  left: `BufError`,\r\n right: `BufError`: Buffer errors might mean we encountered huge headers', /github/home/.cache/Homebrew/cargo_cache/registry/src/github.com-1ecc6299db9ec823/git-odb-0.37.0/src/store_impls/loose/find.rs:156:9\r\n```",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
